tcpdump
Usage: tcpdump [-i IFACE] [-n] [-c N] [-w FILE | -r FILE] [FILTER]

Captures and inspects packets on the wire. Record traffic to a .pcap for later,
or read one back through a filter to find the conversation you care about.

	-i IFACE   capture on this interface ( `lo` is loopback )
	-n         do not resolve names -- faster, and shows raw addresses
	-c N       stop after N packets
	-w FILE    write raw packets to a capture file
	-r FILE    read a capture back instead of the wire
	FILTER     e.g. `tcp port 80`, `host 10.0.0.5 and port 443`

Capture only on networks you own or are authorised to monitor.

See also: masscan, socat
